#: ../../source/assy.rst:59
msgid ""
"One and only one method for placing the object is acceptable. Therefore "
"the sections `location`, `connectPorts` and `connect` are mutually "
"exclusive. Both `connectPorts` and `connect` are used to connect parts to"
" each other by matching their ports. `connect` is universal, while "
"`connectPorts` is specific to connecting with ports and without interface"
" mating."
msgstr ""
"Solo se admite un único método para colocar el objeto. Por lo tanto, las "
"secciones `location`, `connectPorts` y `connect` son mutuamente "
"excluyentes. Tanto `connectPorts` como `connect` se usan para conectar "
"piezas entre sí haciendo coincidir sus puertos. `connect` es universal, "
"mientras que `connectPorts` es específico para conectar con puertos y sin"
" acoplamiento de interfaces."

#: ../../source/assy.rst:64
msgid ""
"The `with` and `to` fields are used to specify the names of interfaces. "
"Where `with` is the interface of the part that is getting added to the "
"assembly, and `to` is the interface of the part that is already in the "
"assembly. The `withInstance` and `toInstance` fields are used to specify "
"the names of interface instances. The `withPort` and `toPort` fields are "
"used to specify the names of ports."
msgstr ""
"Los campos `with` y `to` se usan para especificar los nombres de las "
"interfaces. Donde `with` es la interfaz de la pieza que se está agregando"
" al ensamblaje, y `to` es la interfaz de la pieza que ya está en el "
"ensamblaje. Los campos `withInstance` y `toInstance` se usan para "
"especificar los nombres de las instancias de interfaz. Los campos "
"`withPort` y `toPort` se usan para especificar los nombres de los "
"puertos."

